title: Drainpipe
text: A CONDUIT is a pipe: light passes through it only along its length, and you can't put a piece on it. Run the light along the gutter, down the pipe and out of the spout.
trick: conduits carry light only along their axis and leave just the corners for the reflectors
motif: rain gutter and downpipe
---
L 1 3 2 g
C 2 3 2 k
C 3 3 2 k
C 4 3 2 k
C 5 3 2 k
C 6 3 2 k
C 7 3 2 k
C 8 3 2 k
*R 9 3 7 k
C 10 3 2 k
C 11 3 2 k
C 12 3 2 k
# 13 3 0 k   % end cap of the gutter
C 9 4 0 k
C 9 5 0 k
C 9 6 0 k
